 "api_error_status": null,
 "result": "**Mechanism:** context-local proxies. Each one is a werkzeug `LocalProxy` that looks up the current object through a `ContextVar`.\n\n**Objects involved** (all in `src/tessel/globals.py`):\n- `_app_var` is the `ContextVar` that holds the current `AppContext`.\n- `active_app`, `g`, `request`, `session` and `app_ctx` are `LocalProxy` objects onto `_app_var`. Each one resolves to the matching attribute of the current `AppContext`: the app, its `g` object, the request, and its session.\n\n**Context object:** `AppContext` in `src/tessel/ctx.py`.\n- One context is pushed per request or CLI command.\n- `has_request` says whether the context carries a request.\n- Pushing a context sets `_app_var`, and popping it restores the previous value. That is how each thread or task sees its own objects.\n- `RequestContext` is only a deprecated alias for `AppContext`.\n\nThe `g` class comes from the app's `app_ctx_globals_class` attribute, defined in `src/tessel/sansio/app.py` and `src/tessel/app.py`.",
